.\" man/man3/Docv::Roff::Engine.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Roff::Engine" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Roff::Engine \- The roff interpreter: input stack, requests, strings, macros, registers, conditionals, escapes.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Roff::Engine\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The roff interpreter: input stack, requests, strings, macros, registers,
conditionals, escapes. It drives a native macro package and a \fB\%Builder\fR.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBBREAKING\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
BREAKING = Set {"bp", "br", "brp", "ce", "fi", "nf", "rj", "sp", "in", "ti"}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Requests that cause a break unless called with the no\-break control
character.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBMAX_DEPTH = 120\fR
Maximum nesting of the input stack (macro recursion guard).
.TP 4
\fBMAX_INTERPOLATION = 32\fR
Maximum nesting of string interpolation.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_LOOP = 10000\fR
Maximum iterations of one \fB\%.while\fR loop.
.TP 4
\fBNO_OP\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
NO_OP = Set {"bd", "class", "color", "composite", "cp", "cs", "device", "devicem", "dt", "fam", "fc", "fl", "fspecial", "fzoom", "hc", "hcode", "hla", "hlm", "hpf", "hpfa", "hpfcode", "hw", "hy", "hym", "hys", "kern", "lc", "lf", "lg", "linetabs", "ls", "mc", "mk", "mso", "msoh", "msoquiet", "ne", "nh", "nm", "nn", "nroff", "os", "output", "pc", "pev", "pl", "pline", "pm", "pn", "pnr", "po", "ps", "psbb", "ptr", "pvs", "rt", "shc", "sizes", "special", "spreadwarn", "ss", "sv", "tag", "taga", "tkf", "troff", "uf", "vpt", "vs", "warn", "warnscale", "wh", "ch", "backtrace", "asciify", "unformat", "tc"}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Requests that change nothing on a terminal reflowing viewer: page
geometry and traps, type sizes and spacing, hyphenation, kerning,
ligatures, output devices and debugging output.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBUNSAFE\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
UNSAFE = Set {"sy", "pso", "pi", "open", "opena", "write", "writec", "writem", "close", "cf", "trf", "rd"}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Requests that run commands or access files. They run only with
\fB\%Options#unsafe\fR; otherwise they are accepted and ignored. \fB\%\eV\fR is
gated the same way (see \fB\%interpolate\fR).
.RE
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(source : Source = Source.new, columns : Int32 = 78, options : Options = Options.new)\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef after_next_line : Nil\fR
Runs \fIhook\fR after the next output\-producing input line.
.PP
\fBdef blank_macro : String | Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef blank_macro=(blank_macro : String | Nil)\fR
.PP
\fBdef builder : Builder\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef builtin_register(name : String) : Int64 | Nil\fR
Read\-only and computed registers; \fB\%nil\fR when \fIname\fR is not built in.
.TP 4
\fBdef call_name(name : String, line : String) : Nil\fR
Runs \fIname\fR with an already interpolated argument line (for packages
that call other macros).
.TP 4
\fBdef capture_next_line : Nil\fR
Captures the text of the next input line and hands its spans to
\fIblock\fR (\fB\%.TP\fR tags, \fB\%.SH\fR without arguments).
.TP 4
\fBdef capturing_line? : Bool\fR
True while the next input line is being captured.
.TP 4
\fBdef condition(raw : String) : Tuple(Bool, String)\fR
Splits a conditional into its condition and body and evaluates it.
.TP 4
\fBdef conditional_body(result : Bool, body : String) : Nil\fR
Runs or skips a conditional body (single line or \fB\%\e{ \%... \%\e}\fR block).
.PP
\fBdef control_char=(char : Char) : Char\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef copy_env(name : String) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.evc \%name\fR: copies environment \fIname\fR into the current one.
.TP 4
\fBdef current_args : Array(String)\fR
The arguments of the innermost macro call.
.TP 4
\fBdef defined?(name : String) : Bool\fR
True when \fIname\fR is a user\-defined string or macro.
.TP 4
\fBdef dispatch(name : String, args : String, no_break : Bool = false) : Nil\fR
Runs request, macro or package macro \fIname\fR with raw arguments \fIargs\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef diversion(name : String | Nil, append : Bool) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.di\fR/\fB\%.da\fR/\fB\%.box\fR/\fB\%.boxa\fR: starts diverting input lines into \fIname\fR,
or ends the innermost diversion when \fIname\fR is \fB\%nil\fR.
.PP
\fBdef doc : Document\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef else_branch(raw : String) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.el\fR: runs when the matching \fB\%.ie\fR failed.
.TP 4
\fBdef emit(text : String) : Bool\fR
Formats an interpolated text line into the builder. Returns true when
the line ends with \fB\%\ec\fR (the next input line continues it).
.PP
\fBdef end_macro : String | Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef end_macro=(end_macro : String | Nil)\fR
.PP
\fBdef env : Env\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef env=(env : Env) : Env\fR
Switches the formatting environment.
.TP 4
\fBdef escape_char(char : Char | Nil) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.ec\fR, \fB\%.eo\fR, \fB\%.ecs\fR, \fB\%.ecr\fR.
.PP
\fBdef escapes_off : Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef font_alias(from : String, to : String) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef font_named(name : String) : Font | Nil\fR
Resolves a font name or position through \fB\%.fp\fR and \fB\%.ftr\fR.
.PP
\fBdef font_position(position : String, name : String) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef frame_depth : Int32\fR
Number of frames on the input stack.
.PP
\fBdef glyphs : Hash(String, String)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef halt : Nil\fR
Stops interpretation (\fB\%.ex\fR, \fB\%.ab\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef if_else(raw : String) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.ie\fR: evaluates and remembers the result for \fB\%.el\fR.
.PP
\fBdef input_trap(lines : Int32, handler : String | Nil, continued : Bool) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef interpolate(text : String, copy : Bool, depth : Int32 = 0, braces : Bool = false) : String\fR
Expands strings (\fB\%\e*\fR), registers (\fB\%\en\fR, \fB\%\eg\fR), macro arguments (\fB\%\e$\fR),
widths (\fB\%\ew\fR), \fB\%\eB\fR, \fB\%\eA\fR, \fB\%\eR\fR, \fB\%\eV\fR (environment variables, with
\fB\%Options#unsafe\fR only) and comments. In copy mode (macro
bodies, string values, macro arguments) \fB\%\e\e\fR becomes \fB\%\e\fR, \fB\%\e.\fR becomes
\fB\%.\fR and \fB\%\et\fR/\fB\%\ea\fR become literal characters; other escapes are kept for
the inline formatter.
Conditional braces \fB\%\e{\fR \fB\%\e}\fR are kept only with \fIbraces\fR (macro
bodies, where they still have to delimit blocks when the body runs).
.TP 4
\fBdef invoke(name : String, body : Array(String), args : Array(String)) : Nil\fR
Calls a user macro with \fIargs\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef leave_loop(break_out : Bool) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.break\fR and \fB\%.continue\fR: leave the innermost loop iteration.
.PP
\fBdef macro_body(name : String) : Array(String) | Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef next_file(name : String) : Nil\fR
Continues with \fIname\fR after the current file (\fB\%.nx\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef next_line(floor : Int32) : String | Nil\fR
Reads the next input line from frames above \fIfloor\fR, joining escaped
newlines.
.PP
\fBdef no_break_char=(char : Char) : Char\fR
.PP
\fBdef options : Options\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef plain_text(text : String) : String\fR
Formats \fItext\fR into plain characters without changing any state
(widths, string comparison, headings).
.TP 4
\fBdef pop_env : Nil\fR
\fB\%.ev\fR: returns to the previous environment.
.TP 4
\fBdef process(line : String) : Nil\fR
Interprets one input line.
.TP 4
\fBdef push_env(name : String) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.ev \%name\fR: pushes the current environment and switches.
.TP 4
\fBdef read_body(terminator : String) : Array(String)\fR
Reads a macro body up to \fIterminator\fR in copy mode.
.TP 4
\fBdef read_delimited(reader : Cursor) : String\fR
Reads the argument of an escape delimited by its first character.
.TP 4
\fBdef read_name(reader : Cursor) : String\fR
Reads a one\-character, \fB\%(xx\fR or \fB\%[name]\fR identifier.
.TP 4
\fBdef register_text(name : String, sign : Int32 = 0) : String\fR
The interpolated text of register \fIname\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef register_value(name : String) : Int64\fR
The value of register \fIname\fR (0 when undefined).
.PP
\fBdef registers : Docv::Roff::Registers\fR
.PP
\fBdef remove_macro(name : String) : Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef rename_macro(from : String, to : String) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef request(name : String, raw : String, no_break : Bool) : Bool\fR
Runs a roff request; returns false when \fIname\fR is not a request.
.PP
\fBdef restore_escape : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef return_from_macro : Nil\fR
\fB\%.return\fR: leaves the innermost macro.
.TP 4
\fBdef run(text : String) : Document\fR
Interprets \fItext\fR and returns the document.
.TP 4
\fBdef run_frame(frame : Frame) : Nil\fR
Pushes \fIframe\fR and interprets it until it is exhausted.
.TP 4
\fBdef run_lines(lines : Array(String), kind : Frame::Kind = Frame::Kind::Body) : Nil\fR
Interprets \fIlines\fR as input (macro bodies of packages, conditional
bodies).
.PP
\fBdef save_escape : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef select_font(name : String) : Nil\fR
Sets the font from a name; \fB\%P\fR (or empty) restores the previous one.
.PP
\fBdef set_macro(name : String, body : Array(String)) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef set_register_expression(name : String, expr : String, increment : String | Nil = nil) : Nil\fR
Sets register \fIname\fR from an expression; a leading sign adds to the
current value.
.PP
\fBdef set_string(name : String, value : String) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef shift_args(count : Int32) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.shift \%n\fR: drops the first \fIn\fR macro arguments.
.TP 4
\fBdef skip_until(terminator : String) : Nil\fR
Skips input up to \fIterminator\fR (\fB\%.ig\fR).
.PP
\fBdef source : Source\fR
.PP
\fBdef space_macro : String | Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef space_macro=(space_macro : String | Nil)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef split_args(line : String) : Array(String)\fR
Splits an argument line: blanks separate arguments, double quotes
group them and \fB\%""\fR inside quotes is a literal quote.
.TP 4
\fBdef string(name : String) : String | Nil\fR
The value of string \fIname\fR (macros join their lines).
.TP 4
\fBdef text_line_done(continued : Bool = false) : Nil\fR
Ends an output\-producing input line: word space or break, line
captures, one\-line hooks, centering counts and input traps.
.PP
\fBdef translations : Hash(Char, String)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef while_loop(raw : String) : Nil\fR
\fB\%.while\fR: collects the body and runs it while the condition holds.
